# ista-iq3s-coder:latest — ISTA Qwen3.8-27B IQ3_S sized for a local-model
# (qwen CLI) coder seat. The bare hf.co/...:IQ3_S tag defaults to a small
# context; the SwarmForge coder.md bootstrap alone is ~16k tokens, so the
# first turn dies with exceed_context_size_error under 8192. 32768 was
# still too tight once qwen CLI's own first-turn overhead (~52-55k chars
# with the 6-tool project .qwen/settings.json, BL-1829) is added on top of
# the boot prefix - BL-1801's gate refused every launch. Raised to 49152
# (2026-09-30, operator directive in chat: "augment its max window size if
# 32k is too little") for headroom; kept below a straight double given
# this host's tight RAM (see backlog evidence for the coder@iq3 seat).
# think:false is still required at request time (.qwen/settings.json
# extra_body / Ollama think param).
#
# Apply:  ollama create ista-iq3s-coder:latest -f swarmforge/packs/ista-iq3s-coder.Modelfile
# Use:    window coder local-model coder --model ista-iq3s-coder:latest
# Undo:   point the pack window back at the base hf.co tag; ollama rm ista-iq3s-coder:latest
# num_predict 4096 (2026-09-30, specifier, iq3 absolute-priority hotfix):
# the 12:26Z crash was ONE reply of 9,484 tokens (ollama task 2974) that
# overflowed qwen's then-32768 budget. CORRECTION, same afternoon: this is
# only a default for requests that set no max_tokens, and qwen sets one -
# ollama task 752 generated 8,000+ tokens with it in place. It does NOT cap
# the seat's replies; the 49152 budget (BL-1838) is what gives a long reply
# room. Kept as the default for callers that do not set max_tokens.
# 49152 only fits on the GPU with a q8_0 KV cache (f16 at 49152 is 3 GiB,
# which pushed 8 of 65 layers to the CPU and cut generation from ~18.5 to
# ~3.5 tokens/s): serve with OLLAMA_FLASH_ATTENTION=1 OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q8_0.
FROM hf.co/ISTA-DASLab/Qwen3.8-27B-GSQ-RCO-GGUF:IQ3_S
# Back to 32768 (2026-10-03, specifier hotfix, human: "fix the compression
# trigger first and give iq3 one clean retry"). 49152 sits in qwen's
# compaction dead zone (BL-1840): qwen 0.24.7 compacts at
# min(0.85 x window, window - 20000 - 13000), so 49152 compacts at 16152
# tokens while 32768 compacts at 27852. The seat's prompts ran ~20k tokens,
# so it compacted on EVERY turn, shrinking ~60 tokens each time, and made
# one tool call per 5-10 minutes for 1.5 hours on BL-1916's bounce. The
# 09-30 reason for 49152 no longer holds: the compact local card plus qwen's
# overhead now measures ~12.9k prompt tokens on the first turn (BL-1801's
# fit check passes at 32768). The dead-zone gate refuses 49152, but only a
# full ./swarm launch runs it; a one-seat launch-script regeneration did not.
# The window below, without the vision projector (2026-10-04, specifier; the human:
# "find the sweet spot for the context window ... the size at which the
# coder churns the fastest", then "Ok for the bigger window"). Measured on
# the RTX 5060 Ti 16 GB with q8_0 KV: only 16 of the 64 layers keep a KV
# cache (34 KiB/token), and llama-server keeps 1 GiB of the ~15.0 GB free,
# so without the projector the KV budget is ~73.7k tokens. 65536 and 73728
# run 100% on the GPU at today's speed (decode 27.4 tok/s at 2k, 22.7 at
# 34k; prefill ~800 tok/s). 81920 put 2 of 65 layers on the CPU (decode
# 16.1 -> 10.6) and 98304 4 layers (9.9 -> 6.3). The PARAMETER lines below
# are the one place the window is written: the launch reads it back from
# Ollama, and local_model_window_gate_lib.bb derives qwen's declared window
# and compaction trigger from it (behind the shim qwen compacts 18000 under
# it, from ~61k up sharing the prompt cache). The projector (0.93 GB +
# 248 MiB CLIP compute) is what this window needs; the coder read no image
# in 62 sessions. FROM the hf tag pulls the projector, so apply in two
# steps (the second FROM names only the weights blob, the first FROM line of
# the dumped Modelfile, and copies this file's PARAMETER lines):
#   ollama create ista-iq3s-coder-vision:latest -f swarmforge/packs/ista-iq3s-coder.Modelfile
#   W=$(ollama show --modelfile ista-iq3s-coder-vision:latest | awk '/^FROM \//{print $2; exit}')
#   { sed "s|^FROM .*|FROM $W|" swarmforge/packs/ista-iq3s-coder.Modelfile; echo 'TEMPLATE {{ .Prompt }}'; } > tmp/iq3.Modelfile
#   ollama create ista-iq3s-coder:latest -f tmp/iq3.Modelfile
# The -vision build is a build source only: at this window with its
# projector it spills to the CPU. Kept without vision on trial (the human: "let's try &
# see over time if not having vision is an issue"). If vision is needed:
# with the projector only ~38k fits at q8_0, inside qwen's dead zone, so
# that means back to 32768; untested, OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q4_0 halves KV
# to ~17 KiB/token and should fit this window WITH the projector, at some cost to
# long-context recall, for every model the server runs.
PARAMETER num_ctx 73728
PARAMETER num_predict 4096
